[{"repo_name":"longbridge/openapi","commit_timestamp":"2026-03-09T03:53:39Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"0dbe24a378a9a44092aadb6226c69bc3355b7a96","github_link":"https://github.com/longbridge/openapi/commit/0dbe24a378a9a44092aadb6226c69bc3355b7a96","commit_subject":"docs: move env vars to language READMEs, simplify root Quickstart","ai_tool":"Cursor"},{"repo_name":"PyThaiNLP/pythainlp","commit_timestamp":"2026-03-09T03:48:25Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"11797b90572e92690695f837cce39bc0eeb3c3cf","github_link":"https://github.com/PyThaiNLP/pythainlp/commit/11797b90572e92690695f837cce39bc0eeb3c3cf","commit_subject":"Initial plan","ai_tool":"Copilot"},{"repo_name":"PyThaiNLP/pythainlp","commit_timestamp":"2026-03-09T03:48:24Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"a43ca590ca4a8e1346e32f4ed3acfacefcc1103d","github_link":"https://github.com/PyThaiNLP/pythainlp/commit/a43ca590ca4a8e1346e32f4ed3acfacefcc1103d","commit_subject":"Fix X|Y union type syntax for Python 3.9 compatibility","ai_tool":"Copilot"},{"repo_name":"go-git/go-git","commit_timestamp":"2026-03-09T03:48:18Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"bc7ce77b36e9a2c1125d2a9c6d4876f05cd4f5af","github_link":"https://github.com/go-git/go-git/commit/bc7ce77b36e9a2c1125d2a9c6d4876f05cd4f5af","commit_subject":"git: fix isFastForward for shallow clones When a shallow clone is followed by a depth-limited fetch using a non-force refspec, isFastForward would return plumbing.ErrObjectNotFound because the ancestry walk hit parent commits absent from the local store. The root cause was twofold:   1. All callers passed nil (or only the first shallow commit) to      isFastForward. The function only ever stopped the walk at a single      shallow boundary, leaving every other missing parent reachable (and      therefore causing an object-not-found error).   2. When the ancestry walk cannot reach old within the locally      available history, the only correct interpretation for a shallow      repo is we-do-not-know - not non-fast-forward. Fix:   - Change the isFastForward signature to accept []plumbing.Hash (all     shallow commits) instead of a single *plumbing.Hash.   - Build parentsToIgnore from the parent hashes of ALL shallow commits     so the walk never attempts to load locally absent commits.   - If the walk terminates without finding old and shallows are     present, return (true, nil): the server would not advertise a     non-force ref update that is not a fast-forward, so we conservatively     allow the update - matching git(1) behaviour for shallow fetches.   - Update all callers (remote.go, repository.go, worktree.go) to pass     the full shallow list. checkFastForwardUpdate type-asserts its     storer.EncodedObjectStorer argument to storer.ShallowStorer to     obtain shallows without a signature change. Fixes: https://github.com/go-git/go-git/issues/207","ai_tool":"Copilot"},{"repo_name":"microsoft/aspire","commit_timestamp":"2026-03-09T03:44:57Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"742503378bfa51fb1640599d7432d0124b4fcb58","github_link":"https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/commit/742503378bfa51fb1640599d7432d0124b4fcb58","commit_subject":"Add OpenTelemetry instrumentation to TypeScript starter template (#15051)","ai_tool":"Copilot"},{"repo_name":"mxpv/podsync","commit_timestamp":"2026-03-09T03:44:22Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"ed5f8713658de7d7921537f2061a2610dafc0391","github_link":"https://github.com/mxpv/podsync/commit/ed5f8713658de7d7921537f2061a2610dafc0391","commit_subject":"Remove comment from TestNoListingEnabledWhenConfigured","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"mxpv/podsync","commit_timestamp":"2026-03-09T03:41:32Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"585ed2282343e157e65723373fe0823a601f59da","github_link":"https://github.com/mxpv/podsync/commit/585ed2282343e157e65723373fe0823a601f59da","commit_subject":"Remove misleading NoListing from server test cfg","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"ithewei/libhv","commit_timestamp":"2026-03-09T03:38:39Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"e5d650c7fc4b009